 "verdict": "Today Isaac Lab physics uses no GPU. MPS gave no gain overall: the PPO update is 3.6 times faster (0.29 s against 1.04 s per iteration), but it is about 3.5% of an iteration, and physics takes 28 to 30 s. Whole-iteration throughput was 3254 steps/s on MPS and 3377 on CPU, and that difference is inside the spread of 2 repeats on a shared Mac. The policy alone is faster on the GPU only at large batches: at 128 envs torch on the CPU is faster than MLX on the GPU, and at 4096 envs MLX on the GPU is 6.4 times faster than torch on the CPU.",
